{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q66480924","formula":"C₁₈","hill":"C18","elements":["C"],"composition":{"C":18.0},"names":{"en":"Cyclo[18]carbon","ru":"Цикло(18)углерод"},"descriptions":{"en":"Cyclooctadeca-1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15,17-nonayne or cyclo[18]carbon is an allotrope of carbon with molecular formula C18. The molecule is a ring of eighteen carbon atoms, connected by alternating triple and single bonds; thus, it is a polyyne and a cyclocarbon. Cyclo[18]carbon is the smallest cyclo[n]carbon predicted to be relatively stable, with a computed strain energy of 72 kilocalories per mole.","ru":"1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15,17-циклооктадеканонин или цикло[18]углерод — аллотропная модификация углерода с молекулярной формулой C18. Молекула представляет собой кольцо из восемнадцати атомов углерода, связанных чередующимися тройными и одинарными связями."},"fame":12,"pubchemCid":14940714,"mass":216.2,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1#CC#CC#CC#CC#CC#CC#CC#CC#C1","inchikey":"GPWDPLKISXZVIE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"cyclooctadecanonayne","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"14940714","atoms":18,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.178,"y":-3.701,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.014,"y":-3.563,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.514,"y":-3.382,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.242,"y":-2.95,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":2.515,"y":-2.72,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.068,"y":-2.078,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":3.333,"y":-1.618,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.614,"y":-0.818,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":3.675,"y":-0.467,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.686,"y":0.38,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":3.593,"y":0.903,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.294,"y":1.696,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":3.116,"y":2.005,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.579,"y":2.66,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":2.172,"y":3.002,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.433,"y":3.417,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.098,"y":3.538,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.